        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(memory-wiki): reject malformed ChatGPT timestamps",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\nChatGPT imports accepted malformed Unix timestamp strings like scientific notation or trailing newlines, which could normalize bad source data into valid page timestamps.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\nTightened `isoFromUnix` to only accept finite numeric values or canonical decimal strings, and added a CLI regression test covering malformed ChatGPT timestamp inputs.\n\n## User Impact\nChatGPT imports now reject malformed timestamp text instead of silently accepting it. Valid imports are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n- Current head `91803751d2547a0672fb39696a3c7f9fd032cb18`: real import proof via `node --import tsx --input-type=module -` running `importChatGptConversations` on a synthetic ChatGPT export with one canonical decimal timestamp and one malformed scientific-notation timestamp with a trailing newline. The malformed record stayed at `Created = Updated = 2024-04-06T01:20:00.000Z`; the canonical record advanced `Updated` to `2024-04-06T01:40:00.000Z`.",
